                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[b]Invisible Apartment 2[/b] is a short cyberpunk themed [b]Visual Novel[/b] taking place in a mega city, which is completely under surveillance of government & corporations, where hacking is a part of every day life for a lot of people.\n\nThe story follows events from the first game. It mostly shows life of Kacey and her AI companion, whose interactions show a bit of emotional depth. Their goal is to hack and gain access to highly classified data that’s locked up in Central Authority Network. World build in the game captures pretty well a cyberpunk atmosphere with a constant government surveillance and strong resistance of common people to corporate greed and control.\nThe game might be short, but I don’t find that as an issue. Not every story has to be 30+ hours long. And if you want to get the full experience, there are different paths with dialogue choices that can lead to either good or bad ending.\n\nTo conclude this short review, I’d say it’s definitely worth a try for people who are into cyberpunk theme in their media.\n\nPlayed the game on YouTube very long time ago. You can watch the entire thing from my [url=https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLF6bMpb7g7_RofvGpOkVnfo_mqCJ_xes0][b]Invisible Apartment 2 playlist[/b][/url].",
